# Mimi Studio — project context

## Product one-liner

**Mimi** is a private AI editorial studio that turns scattered creative evidence into an approved **Taste Graph** — traceable direction for zines, dossiers, identity projections, and image-making. The creator approves what becomes memory; outputs show **Used Context**, not hidden chat history.

Workflow grammar: **Capture → Interpret → Approve → Remember → Retrieve → Generate → Compose → Export**.

## Stack

| Layer | Technology |
| --- | --- |
| UI | React 19, TypeScript, Vite, Framer Motion |
| Server | Express (`server.ts` + `tsx`), Vite middleware in dev, `/api/*` routes |
| Auth & private state | Firebase Auth, Firestore, Firebase Admin |
| Owned public plane | Sovereign archive (SQLite local / Postgres-Neon on Vercel) |
| AI | Google Gemini, Vercel AI Gateway (`modelFor` / `services/modelConfig.ts`) |
| Billing | Stripe |
| Deploy | Netlify / Vercel-compatible Express host |
| Tests | Playwright E2E, canon validation scripts |

Single process: `npm run dev` serves SPA + API on one port (default `:3000`).

## Design constraints

- **Display type:** Cormorant Garamond (`font-display`, `font-serif`, `font-header`).
- **UI sans:** DM Sans for humanist UI copy where specified; default shell sans is Geist Variable (migrate toward DM Sans on new surfaces when choosing fonts).
- **Palette:** parchment / archival — use CSS variables and Tailwind `mimi.*` / `nous.*` tokens only (`--mimi-field`, `--mimi-ink`, `--mimi-olive`, `--mimi-stone`, `--mimi-hairline`, `--mimi-cobalt`, manila tokens). See `docs/house-style-v2.md` and `index.css`.
- **No hardcoded hex in components** — theme tokens only. Tailwind `archival.*` literals are legacy; prefer `mimi.*` / CSS vars on new code.
- **Brand:** readable **Mimi** (title case). Never render `MIMI` via CSS `uppercase` on brand strings.
- **Shells:** shared Studio OS (`components/studio-os/`), `lib/productCanon.ts`, `lib/design-system.ts`. Bottom anchors: Map · Mimi seal · Find — no permanent multi-chamber tab bar.
- **Motion / haptics:** `useFeedback()` semantic events only (`lib/feedback/`).
- **Honest states:** empty ≠ done; storage error ≠ delete; demonstration data must be labeled.

Full UX preferences: `.cursor/skills/mimi-product-preferences/SKILL.md`.

## Routing — server-visible HTML

All **new routes** (especially public faces, share cards, feeds, OG/Twitter previews) must return **server-visible HTML**:

1. Register an Express `app.get` handler (or extend an existing one) that reads `index.html` / `dist/index.html`.
2. Inject route-specific `<title>`, description, and Open Graph / Twitter meta before send (pattern: `/s/:zineId` in `server.ts` → `injectZineSEOMetadata`).
3. In dev, run `viteInstance.transformIndexHtml` when Vite is available.
4. Do not rely on client-only rendering for crawlable/share preview content.

Infrastructure routes (`/u/:handle`, `/s/:id`, `/u/:handle/feed.xml`, `/api/feed`) already follow this contract.

## Living documentation — mandatory updates

At the end of any task that **changes architecture** or **ships / materially upgrades a module**:

1. Update `docs/STATE.md` — module status (`stub` / `partial` / `shipped`), known debt, next action.
2. Append to `docs/DECISIONS.md` — date, decision, alternatives rejected, rationale (ADR-lite).

**Do not ask permission** to update these files when the above conditions apply.

Reference docs: `docs/STRATEGY.md` (positioning & quarter scope), `docs/mimi-system-architecture.md` (canonical architecture), `lib/productCanon.ts` (chamber registry).
